From 14bf1b0aedb3bc7459329dd01e9652c425241421 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cerXXXX <84661580+cerXXXX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:55:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: --eco holds the wallpaper still and shows a frame only
 when it changes

--eco: once the first frame has been up for a second, the animation time
stops (particles, shaders, texture animations, videos pause) while
scripts keep reading the real time. Every second, just after the second
changes (timerfd, re-aligned when the clock jumps), the frame is rendered
and hashed, and only shown when it differs: a clock with seconds updates
every second, one without once a minute, a wallpaper without clocks
never. Frame callbacks don't drive rendering while held.

--control reads commands from stdin: "eco on|off", "fps <n>", "mute on|off",
so a running wallpaper switches modes without being restarted.

--frame-file renders in a hidden window (like --stream) and writes each
changed frame as PPM, printing "Frame written" (the lock screen in eco).

Sound fades out (0.5 s) instead of being cut when muted or when another
app plays, and comes back 2 s after it stopped. The detector now finds
the process of native PipeWire streams through their client (it never
saw any before), ignores paused streams and other wallpapers, and checks
at most every 250 ms. The SDL device is paused while there's nothing to
hear, so the sound card can sleep (it played silence even with --silent).

